// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// coop_dialog.cpp -- Round 7 dialogue + cinematics lane (gaps G8 / G10).
//
// Round 7b (owner decisions) makes the peer a PARTICIPANT, not a spectator:
//
//   CINEMA.  When A plays a level sequence, B plays the SAME sequence locally at
//   the same moment (a late join tries to jump to A's position), and a skip/end on
//   either side ends it for both.  Both players get the game's own treatment:
//   player hidden, input and movement locked, camera driven by the sequence.
//   B's copy has BroadcastEventAfterCinematic cleared, so the world effect
//   (GlobalEvent / quest consequences) still happens exactly ONCE, through the
//   existing sync.
//
//   DIALOGUE.  B hears A's conversation and sees its subtitles, driven by A's
//   nodes -- B never starts an independent conversation and never applies an
//   outcome itself (narrative tags / quests / PlayerChoice arrive through the
//   existing sync).  At a choice node EVERY player votes; the owner (the player
//   who started the conversation) resolves: most votes wins, a tie between
//   different options goes to the HOST's vote, the window closes when everybody
//   has voted or after `[Rules] dialog_vote_timeout` seconds (20 s default), a
//   peer that is out of zone / absent abstains immediately, nobody voting leaves
//   the game's own default (option 0).  The owner then applies the winner through
//   the game's own select call, ONCE.
//
// WHAT THE GAME DOES (dump-proved offsets):
//   UDialogueSubsystem (UWorldSubsystem): ActiveDialogues: TArray<FActiveDialogue>
//   @0x00A0; FActiveDialogue is 0x88: Instigator @+0x00, DialogueContext @+0x08,
//   DialogueAsset @+0x10, Tags @+0x18, BlockingTags @+0x38, SoundComp @+0x68,
//   FacialAnimationInstance @+0x70, FacialAnimationMontage @+0x78.
//   UDlgContext: GetActiveNodeIndex, GetOptionsNum, ChooseOption(int32),
//   ChooseChild, ChooseSpeechSequenceOptionFromReplicated(int32).
//   UDlgDialogue: Nodes: TArray<UDlgNode*> @0x170.  UDlgNode::Children:
//   TArray<FDlgEdge> @0x88 and FDlgEdge{TargetIndex @0x0, Text @0x30 (FText), size
//   0x60} -- the option labels.  UDialogue_SpartaSpeechNode: Text @0xA0 (FText),
//   SoundWave @0xD0, AudioEvent @0xF8, SubtitleSpeakerName @0x114.  That is how the
//   LISTENER gets the very same line text and voice asset with no string the mod
//   had to build.
//   ABP_CinematicPlayer_C: CutsceneActor @0x2C0, LevelSequenceToPlay @0x2C8,
//   BroadcastEventAfterCinematic @0x2F8, ThisCinematicTag @0x320, StateGE @0x3A0,
//   Skippable @0x3B0; functions PrepareCutscene/PlayCutscene/EndCutscene/
//   ForceStopCinematic (no params).  ABP_DialogueActor_C / ABP_NPC_C hold the
//   `Dialogue Instigator Component` (BPC_DialogueInstigator_C: DlgDialogue @0x148,
//   Participants @0x150, bDisablePlayerInput @0x194) whose
//   StartDialogue(3 tag containers, out Success) is the game's own way to start a
//   conversation -- `dlgstart` uses it.
//
// WIRE (own top-level keys, appended LAST so no existing key moves):
//   ,"dl":[<active>,<seq>,<node>,<opts>,"<dlgName>","<dlgAssetPath>"]
//   ,"ct":[<outSeq>,"<PlayerChoice>"]
//   ,"ci":[<active>,<seq>,<elapsedMs>,"<sequenceName>"]
//   ,"dv":[<dSeq>,<node>,<opt>,"<playerId>"]          one vote   (repeated 4 s)
//   ,"dr":[<dSeq>,<node>,<winner>,"<id:opt|id:opt>"]  resolution (repeated 6 s)
// Every one carries a sequence/number and is repeated for a few seconds, so a lost
// or repeated packet is harmless (R7 wire rule); sections are only emitted while
// they are (or just were) non-zero.
//
// Kill switches: DIALOG_OFF.txt, CINE_OFF.txt.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

