// How long a "not busy any more" notice keeps riding every packet after the
// dialogue / cinematic ends.  It has to OUTLIVE the receiver's own bad moment: the
// end of a cutscene raises the game's loading screen for 1-3 s, which arms a hard
// ready loss (kLocalHoldSecs = 3 s) and skips ApplyPeer there, so a 4 s repeat could
// be swallowed whole -- measured: B kept replaying after `cinestop` (CINE
// endedBoth=False) and A lost the fresh `bh` (PEERHP stale).  8 s covers the hold
// with margin; a repeated notice is harmless (every copy carries its seq).
